# Every deployment target here is Linux (GCE COS images, Docker containers).
# Several .tf modules embed shell startup-scripts as heredocs — CRLF in one
# of those corrupts the shebang line (`/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter`) and
# the script fails before its first real command, silently (GCE just marks
# the startup-scripts service as failed; nothing here surfaces it). Force
# LF for all text files regardless of a contributor's local core.autocrlf,
# so a Windows checkout can't reintroduce this.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.xlsx binary
